Conclusion
In this lab, you used Ansible to automate the full lifecycle of an Apache HTTP Server deployment: installing the software, configuring multiple virtual hosts with dedicated document roots, deploying custom error pages, and building a dedicated test playbook to validate the result. You practiced core Ansible concepts including inventories, variables files, Jinja2 templates, handlers, and the uri and wait_for modules for validation, while also learning to read Ansible task output and Apache's own httpd -t syntax checker to confirm a deployment is healthy. The troubleshooting steps covered here, checking service status, firewall rules, SELinux, and virtual host routing, reflect the same diagnostic process used in production web server administration. From here, you can extend this project by adding real SSL/TLS certificates from a certificate authority, integrating Ansible Vault to protect sensitive variables, or converting these playbooks into reusable Ansible roles for larger, multi-environment deployments.
